{:event/id "015b2ec2-142d-4b06-a725-ee190787c54a" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:32e0bd69-cf1a-4e16-94e1-136861ee92d4" :event/seq 1 :event/causes ["32e0bd69-cf1a-4e16-94e1-136861ee92d4"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:32e0bd69-cf1a-4e16-94e1-136861ee92d4" :event/at "2026-09-07T13:19:30Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/scope-declaration-is-flat-capability-projection :finding/shapes #{:scope :projection :resolver :capability} :finding/current-name "knoxx.backend.domain.action.registry/resolve-scope + katamorph.action.interpreter/resolve-scope-decl" :finding/candidate-name "DeclaredCapabilityScope<Id,Capability>" :finding/claim "An action scope declaration projects declared ids into one flat runtime capability map; it is neither a registry nor a transitive closure. Declared action ids become late-bound dispatch trampolines even when the target is absent at resolution time, while missing filters and stores are omitted by Katamorph. An explicit action-local scope overrides registered scope metadata. Presence in scope therefore proves declared authority/name, not current target existence, and the category-specific resolution laws must remain visible."}}
{:event/id "6583421c-150b-45af-8f83-aa240823c3af" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:32e0bd69-cf1a-4e16-94e1-136861ee92d4" :event/seq 2 :event/causes ["015b2ec2-142d-4b06-a725-ee190787c54a"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:32e0bd69-cf1a-4e16-94e1-136861ee92d4" :event/at "2026-09-07T13:19:30Z" :event/data {:finding/id :foresight/executable-registries-are-process-local-lww :finding/shapes #{:registry :capability :runtime :dispatch} :finding/current-name "Knoxx action-registry* + Katamorph drivers*" :finding/candidate-name "ExecutableRegistry<Key,Impl>" :finding/claim "Knoxx action registration and Katamorph driver registration independently use process-local keyed maps with last-write-wins replacement to hold executable implementations and derive lookup/list views from current state. Action entries carry handler metadata and hybrid multimethod dispatch, while drivers satisfy the EventDriver protocol and normalize source events; the shared law is mutable implementation registration, not a universal dispatcher or protocol."}}
{:event/id "0a8662d7-812a-4092-9c55-4581401c868a" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:32e0bd69-cf1a-4e16-94e1-136861ee92d4" :event/seq 3 :event/causes ["6583421c-150b-45af-8f83-aa240823c3af"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:32e0bd69-cf1a-4e16-94e1-136861ee92d4" :event/at "2026-09-07T13:19:30Z" :event/data {:finding/id :katamorph/resource-registry-is-read-catalog :finding/shapes #{:registry :resource :catalog :protocol} :finding/current-name "katamorph.registry.resource/Registry + EdnResourceRegistry" :finding/candidate-name "ResourceCatalog<Kind,Id>" :finding/claim "Katamorph resource registries are fixed per-kind catalog capabilities that delegate list/get to injected resource operations; they neither own mutable implementation state nor execute resources. One protocol is instantiated across eleven resource kinds and Knoxx re-exports it as a compatibility surface. Calling this and ExecutableRegistry by the same unqualified name Registry hides materially different ownership and mutation laws."}}
